{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Better.</b> Having finished explaining that the affair of the fool, even if he has great wealth, is vanity, he mentioned that the better one is the wise man, even if he be poor. For מסכן is like דל, as in אשר לא במסכנות (who was not in poverty). And a youth corresponds to an old and poor man; a wise man corresponds to a fool. And the meaning of youth is that every day he adds wisdom, and the old man no longer knows to be careful, because he is old in his folly."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:33.294162597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}